  <static seed="1929" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers40.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p>Do not use a calculator.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{64} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{0.64} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{6400} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.8</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>80</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>First, recognize that <m>64</m> is a square number. Since <m>8\cdot8=64</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{64}=8</m>.</p>
<p>Next, since <m>0.8\cdot0.8=0.64</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{0.64}=0.8</m>.</p>
<p>Finally, since <m>80\cdot80=6400</m>, we have <m>\sqrt{6400}=80</m>.</p>
</solution>
